  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluate the Integral by substitution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the antiderivative</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle\int{@func@}\,d{@tt@}\)</p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Let us solve \(\displaystyle \int {@func@}\, d{@tt@}\) by substitution method.</p>
<p>let \(u= \displaystyle {@us@} \)</p>
<p>Differentiating \(u\) with respect to \({@tt@}\) yields to \(\frac{du}{d{@tt@}}={@bb@}\). Then \(d{@tt@}=\frac{du}{@bb@}\)</p>
<p>Replacing \(u\) and \(d{@tt@}\) expressions into the original integral yields;</p>
<p>\[ \displaystyle \int {@func@}\, d{@tt@} = \displaystyle \int {@func_u@}\, du = {@tas@} \]</p>

<p>Substituting the expression corresponding to \(u\) into \( \displaystyle {@tas@}\) yields to:</p>
<p>\[ \displaystyle \int {@func@}\, d{@tt@} = {@ta_1@} \]<br></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
